  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The conditional conservation and error calculation is supported, but equivalence of the unrestricted routine interface to the interpreted Riemann workflow is not established. The final classification is undetermined, without majority voting.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 5, paragraph following (1.11), obtains information by solving the Riemann problem. D027 requires only domain, solve, extract, and numericalFlux functions; the complete target supplies physical comparisons only conditionally."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The requested issues have been separated into operator meaning, applicability, nonvacuity, and process correspondence. Native declaration evidence resolves operator meaning and concrete nonvacuity; it does not by itself resolve source correspondence.",
      "primary_evidence": "D014, D026, D027, and the supplied native measure, norm, and actual_two_face_source_application declarations."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Uncertainty is retained specifically for full forward correspondence. It is not retained for the signs, normalization, norm semantics, algebraic estimates, or existence of meaningful instances.",
      "primary_evidence": "The complete target states the signed error identity and both conditional estimates explicitly; D022 and D023 fix their update and normalization."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "The Lean types are unambiguous: positive finite real dimension, an arbitrary admissible set, and a total ambient flux differentiable with a complete real eigenbasis at admissible states. Finite vectors fit the source. Coverage of every intended source state-domain model by this ambient representation remains unestablished.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001, D024, D025, D030, D172, and D177; printed pages 4–5 describe vector conserved quantities and hyperbolic equations without specifying this exact domain representation."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C03 unclear",
      "resolution": "The existential routine is chosen for each law and bias before its problems are quantified. The arbitrary-routine branch is independent of that witness. References and bounds are universally quantified conditional inputs, not produced witnesses. These quantifiers support conditional estimates but cannot establish reference availability.",
      "primary_evidence": "The fully explicit target has Exists available, Exists admitted, then forall problem in its first conjunct, and forall leftReference rightReference in its final clause."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "Positive cell width, positive duration, integrability, and the assumed local rectangle balance are appropriate under Q7 and the applicable rectangle portion of the inherited receipt. Reference requirements are additional conditions on optional comparison inputs, not premises of routine execution or the direct error estimate.",
      "primary_evidence": "The complete target places the direct estimate before universal reference quantification. D026 confines conservation obligations to times between zero and problem.duration."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "All selected quantitative error-propagation conclusions are present. Separate shock-formation, classical-solution, and typical-wave assertions are contextual here. Whether the remaining source requirement of obtaining information through a Riemann solve is fully represented remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 5, Section 1.2 and the paragraph following (1.11); the complete target includes normalization, both face compositions, the update identity, and direct and reference-split bounds."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C08 unclear",
      "resolution": "Physical states, physical fluxes, numerical data, routine results, reference means, and updated values remain distinct. However, naming an unconstrained function solve does not establish that its result represents solving or approximating the Riemann problem.",
      "primary_evidence": "D018 composes three functions; D027 contains no semantic correctness field. The target separately compares numerical fluxes with actual physical means and optional reference means."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The local one-cell, two-face formulation does not impose a uniform or global grid. Optional references are global in space but finite in their constrained time horizon. These restrictions must not be called stronger source results; full coverage of intended source reference and state-domain models has not been demonstrated.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target quantifies a<b and s<t without a mesh type. D026 quantifies all spatial endpoints and only 0≤s≤t≤duration. The recorded receipts do not authorize global solution extensions."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "The initial value at the jump remains unrestricted, and positive lengths exclude degenerate normalization. Positive-time face means do depend on the chosen field representative. The target assumes the corresponding balance instead of proving representative independence, so no such independence can be credited.",
      "primary_evidence": "D003 specifies only x<0 and x>0. D014 evaluates flux at reference.field 0 τ. D026 imposes rectangle balance using field values at every endpoint. Printed pages 4–5 leave trace conventions implicit."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C12 unclear",
      "resolution": "The theorem is not wholly vacuous. The supplied native application instantiates the actual target with positive dimension, admitted problems, physical balance, and available references. This establishes concrete applicability, but not reference existence for every hyperbolic problem.",
      "primary_evidence": "LocalRoutineApplicability.actual_two_face_source_application and actual_reference_and_nonconsistency, together with BiasedLocalRiemannRoutine.reference and equal_state_error."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N01 unclear",
      "resolution": "The execution chain is explicit and the computed face fluxes really enter the update. Q7 authorizes information-only results and independently conditional accuracy. It does not explicitly identify every arbitrary input-output routine with an exact or approximate Riemann solver. That distinction remains the principal unresolved correspondence issue.",
      "primary_evidence": "D018 and D022 establish the composition and update. The native biasedRoutine definition simply returns the input pair and computes f(left)+bias. Printed pages 5–6 describe solving Riemann problems and using approximate Riemann solvers."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The target asserts neither universal Riemann solution existence nor uniqueness, entropy admissibility, or accurate-solver existence. Optional reference hypotheses therefore do not make its algebra false or its direct estimate inapplicable. Whether the selected workflow requires a stronger existence or solution linkage than this bare interface remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "D025 bundles hyperbolicity only; D027 has no reference field; references occur universally in the final target clause. The source passage gives no precise universal well-posedness theorem."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "The forward implication remains unclear for the complete interpreted workflow. It is established for normalization, orientation, execution composition, and conditional error propagation, but not for the source meaning of Riemann-solution information.",
      "primary_evidence": "Q7 permits information-only exact or approximate routines. D027 permits arbitrary routines, and no target conclusion supplies a reference or establishes solver correctness."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "The reverse direction is supported under the recorded interpretation and the explicit formal definitions. The target's assertions follow from its local balance and bounds by algebra and norm inequalities; its extra routine witness is directly constructible. This does not establish that the formal interface exhausts the source meaning.",
      "primary_evidence": "D027 permits domain=True, solve returning the ordered pair, identity extraction, and numericalFlux=f(first)+bias. D022–D023 and the assumed rectangle balance give the error identity; the supplied norm declarations identify a genuine finite maximum norm."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected Q7 interpretation and the applicable rectangle/integrability portion of the inherited user receipt, Lean supplies the required normalized conservative update and propagation of independent physical errors. It also supplies an explicit information pipeline. However, Routine contains no condition establishing exact or approximate Riemann solving, and the existential biased witness certifies only that this interface is inhabited. Universal conditional reference comparisons do not provide reference existence or a solution-to-output relation. Q7 clearly removes a compulsory returned field and unconditional accuracy guarantee, but does not explicitly remove the Riemann-solving meaning itself. Full forward correspondence therefore remains uncertain."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Under Q7, the applicable inherited rectangle convention, and the supplied formal definitions, the entire Lean conclusion follows with its stated conditional scope. Write h=b-a>0 and k=t-s>0. Rectangle balance gives h(Q1-Q0)=k(PL-PR), and the defined update gives h(N-Q1)=h(C-Q0)+k((FL-PL)-(FR-PR)). The triangle inequality and positive scaling yield the direct bound; splitting each face discrepancy through a supplied reference mean yields the final bound. Reference certifications follow from D026 and D014. The additional total biased routine is constructible using D027 without any physical existence assertion. These are interpretation-qualified mathematical consequences, not quantitative claims printed in Chapter 1."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "Whether Q7's information-only exact-or-approximate Riemann workflow is intended to be exhausted by an unrestricted routine interface with only independently assumed output-error bounds.",
    "Whether every intended source state-domain and reference-solution model can be represented by the total ambient flux and pointwise-endpoint Reference contracts without reducing applicability.",
    "The printed source's endpoint-trace and representative conventions remain unspecified; neither recorded interpretation establishes representative independence."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-riemann-process-correspondence",
      "evidence": "Printed page 5 obtains information by solving the Riemann problem. D027 has no correctness relation; the native biasedRoutine returns the original state pair and computes f(left)+bias. The target's references are conditional universal inputs.",
      "impact": "The direct judge's equivalence verdict requires an interpretation of Q7 that is not explicit in the supplied convention. Mathematical validity of the error bound alone does not settle this correspondence."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "verified-operators-and-error-propagation",
      "evidence": "D022–D023 preserve normalization and signs. The native supplement identifies standard real volume, the integrable Bochner integral, and the maximum absolute component norm, including agreement between the norm and integrability instance paths.",
      "impact": "No unresolved measure scaling, norm substitution, zero-denominator artifact, or flux-sign defect remains in the conditional estimates."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "nonvacuity-with-limited-coverage",
      "evidence": "The supplied native actual-target application has positive dimension and admitted face problems; separate declarations provide references and a nonzero face error of 1/2.",
      "impact": "Empty domains do not explain the theorem's validity. These witnesses establish concrete applicability without establishing universal solver or reference availability."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "interpretation-authority",
      "evidence": "Q7 separately selects conditional error bounds. The inherited user's literal adoption concerns Chapter 1 rectangle conservation and preserves source ambiguity.",
      "impact": "Neither convention is attributed to the printed book, expanded into a universal existence theorem, or treated as a requested acceptance verdict."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "I inspected the attached primary-source renderings and the supplied declaration, translation, judgment, and native evidence without accessing tools or recomputing hashes. The algebraic and operator issues are resolved positively, and concrete nonvacuity is established. Optional reference restrictions do not invalidate the direct conditional estimate, but their conditional placement also cannot establish source-wide reference coverage. The decisive remaining issue is whether the authorized information-only interpretation preserves enough Riemann-solving content through an otherwise unrestricted routine. Because that correspondence is not established, faithful-equivalent and faithful-stronger are not justified. The reverse mathematical implication is supported; the forward semantic implication remains unclear, consistently yielding undetermined."
}
